# Completed transaction

The publishing completed-transaction template is a service feedback destination after a transaction; it is not simply a generic success panel. [Official publishing guidance](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/frontend-templates/completed-transaction/).

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation; they do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## When to use it

In Home Assistant, distinguish a command being accepted from a device reaching the requested state. A completed setup flow can show what was saved and the useful next action. Feedback should be optional and separate from the confirmed result.

## Structure and behaviour

Name the completed task, include a reference only if the underlying system provides one, and explain any remaining work. A request still awaiting the device should say so. Retain a route back to the relevant native page. A short action may need a local status message rather than a whole completion page.

## Home Assistant boundary

No government /done route, satisfaction service or promotional content is added. The examples are explicitly fictional outcome states and do not call devices. Never show “Completed” merely because the user pressed a button or the visual animation ended.

